Recommended Next Step: Service Worker & Offline Caching
This is a core PWA requirement and will allow users to:

Access previously loaded articles offline.

See “Offline available” badges in the Library.

Use the cache strategies you designed (cache-first, network-first, stale-while-revalidate).

We’ll implement:

Register a service worker (using Next.js’s built‑in next-pwa or a custom setup).

Cache static assets (JS, CSS, fonts) using a cache-first strategy.

Cache article data from the API using the selected cache strategy (you already have the UI for selecting it).

Show real offline availability in the Library – based on whether the article’s data is in the cache.

Update the offline indicator to reflect real network status and pending sync.

